{"total_count": 29, "incomplete_results": false, "items": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/355", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/355/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/355/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/355/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/355", "id": 4933425200, "node_id": "PR_kwDOG9EFvM70Ewlz", "number": 355, "title": "fix: catch OverflowError in naturalsize() for very large integers", "user": {"login": "koteshyelamati", "id": 196373335, "node_id": "U_kgDOC7RrVw", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196373335?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati", "html_url": "https://github.com/koteshyelamati", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/koteshyelamati/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2026-07-20T22:00:39Z", "updated_at": "2026-07-20T22:00:39Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/pulls/355", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/355", "diff_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/355.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/355.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\n`naturalsize()` calls `float(value)` unconditionally, which raises `OverflowError` for very large integers:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n>>> import humanize\r\n>>> humanize.naturalsize(10**309)\r\nOverflowError: int too large to convert to float\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt also raises a raw `ValueError` from `float()` for non-numeric strings, with a confusing message.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nWrap `float(value)` in `try/except (ValueError, OverflowError)` and re-raise with a clear message indicating the argument type.\r\n\r\n## After fix\r\n\r\n```python\r\n>>> humanize.naturalsize(10**309)\r\nValueError: naturalsize() argument must be a number, not 'int'\r\n>>> humanize.naturalsize(\"abc\")\r\nValueError: naturalsize() argument must be a number, not 'str'\r\n```", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/355/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/355/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/366", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/366/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/366/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/366/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/issues/366", "id": 5027738049, "node_id": "I_kwDOG9EFvM8AAAABK60xwQ", "number": 366, "title": "`naturalsize()` raises `ValueError` for custom format strings with text", "user": {"login": "APITester26", "id": 311281201, "node_id": "U_kgDOEo3GMQ", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/311281201?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26", "html_url": "https://github.com/APITester26", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/APITester26/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2026-07-31T08:07:06Z", "updated_at": "2026-07-31T08:07:06Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "## Environment\n\n- humanize 4.16.0 and current `main` at `42b4a1db`\n- Python 3.11.15\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```python\nimport humanize\n\nprint(humanize.naturalsize(999_999, gnu=True, format=\"Size: %.1f\"))\n```\n\nhumanize 4.15.0 returns:\n\n```text\nSize: 976.6K\n```\n\nhumanize 4.16.0 and current `main` raise:\n\n```text\nValueError: could not convert string to float: 'Size: 976.6'\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nThe documented custom formatter should continue to accept text around the numeric conversion.\nSince this behavior worked in 4.15.0, preserving it would avoid a backward compatibility regression.\n\n## Cause\n\nPR #329 added unit rollover handling. The new condition formats the mantissa with the\nuser-provided format and passes the entire result to `float()`:\n\n```python\nfloat(format % (abs_bytes / (base**exp)))\n```\n\nThis works for a plain numeric format such as `\"%.1f\"`, but not for a general formatter\nsuch as `\"Size: %.1f\"`.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nIt might be preferable not to require the complete user-formatted result to be parseable as a float. One\nbackward-compatible option is to apply rollover only when the formatted result is a\nplain numeric string, and otherwise preserve the pre-4.16 behavior. A more complete\nsolution could derive the rounded numeric mantissa independently from surrounding text.\n\nIt might also be worth adding a regression test covering both a prefix and a suffix.\n\n## How this was found\n\nThis was found by change-directed differential testing: reviewing the recent rollover change, mapping it to the public `naturalsize() API`, and constructing a documented custom formatter that reaches the newly added `float(format % value)` expression.\n\nRelated: #329, which fixes rollover but does not discuss custom format strings.\n\nThanks for taking the time to review this report! I appreciate all the work that goes into maintaining this project.", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/366/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/366/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "pinned_comment": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/367", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/367/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/367/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/367/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/367", "id": 5032303454, "node_id": "PR_kwDOG9EFvM75Jdky", "number": 367, "title": "Fix naturalsize() ValueError for custom formats containing text", "user": {"login": "Sanjays2402", "id": 51058514, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDU4NTE0", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51058514?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402", "html_url": "https://github.com/Sanjays2402", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sanjays2402/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2026-07-31T18:24:20Z", "updated_at": "2026-07-31T18:24:20Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/pulls/367", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/367", "diff_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/367.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/367.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "Fixes #366\n\nChanges proposed in this pull request:\n\n* `naturalsize()`'s unit-rollover check ran the user-supplied `format` through `float()`, so any format with text around the conversion (e.g. `\"Size: %.1f\"`) raised `ValueError` — a regression from 4.15.0.\n* Compare the rendered mantissa against the rendered base instead, keeping the 999999 -> `1.0 MB` carry-over while accepting arbitrary formats again.\n* Added two parametrized cases to `tests/test_filesize.py`; they fail with `ValueError` without the fix and pass with it.\n\nThis change was prepared with AI assistance; the regression test was run locally and fails without the fix.\n", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/367/reactions", "total_count": 1, "+1": 1, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/367/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/299", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/299/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/299/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/299/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/299", "id": 4007254133, "node_id": "PR_kwDOG9EFvM7HIR02", "number": 299, "title": "Handle NaN/Inf in naturalsize", "user": {"login": "shuofengzhang", "id": 24763026, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI0NzYzMDI2", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24763026?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang", "html_url": "https://github.com/shuofengzhang", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/shuofengzhang/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [{"id": 4034495679, "node_id": "LA_kwDOG9EFvM7weYS_", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/labels/changelog:%20Added", "name": "changelog: Added", "color": "0e8a16", "default": false, "description": "For new features"}], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 3, "created_at": "2026-03-01T13:52:12Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-24T19:23:42Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/pulls/299", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/299", "diff_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/299.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/299.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "## What changed\n- Return a clear string for non‑finite inputs (NaN/±Inf) in `naturalsize()`.\n- Add tests covering NaN and ±Inf.\n\n## Why\n- `naturalsize()` currently computes logs on non‑finite inputs, which yields confusing output.\n- This aligns with other humanize helpers that render NaN/Inf explicitly.\n\n## Testing\n- ✅ `pytest -q`\n", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/299/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/299/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/378", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/378/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/378/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/378/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/378", "id": 5172298206, "node_id": "PR_kwDOG9EFvM8AAAABABlIAA", "number": 378, "title": "Use a comma as the fr_FR decimal separator", "user": {"login": "ckarnell", "id": 7363269, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjczNjMyNjk=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7363269?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell", "html_url": "https://github.com/ckarnell", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ckarnell/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2026-08-17T13:16:19Z", "updated_at": "2026-08-17T13:16:19Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/pulls/378", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/378", "diff_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/378.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/378.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "`fr_FR` is the only entry in `_DECIMAL_SEPARATOR` with a dot. Every other locale there pairs a group separator with a comma, including `hu_HU` and `lv`, which group with a space exactly like French does.\n\n```python\nhumanize.i18n.activate(\"fr_FR\")\nhumanize.intcomma(1_234_567.89)   # \"1 234 567.89\", want \"1 234 567,89\"\nhumanize.intword(1_000)           # \"1.0 mille\",    want \"1,0 mille\"\n```\n\nYou already worked this out in #357: the dot came from #248, and merwok said French needs the comma. That PR was closed by its author before it landed. So the value is still there.\n\nOne line of data. Plus the 26 fr_FR expectations that encoded the old output.\n\n`naturalsize` is deliberately untouched, and it is the one loose end. `filesize.py` never reads the separator, so it still prints `42.0 Ko` while `intcomma` now prints a comma. #357 tried to fix both together and picked up a 10% performance report on the bundle, so this leaves that half alone. Happy to send it separately if you want it, and it's a fair reason to hold this one.\n\nTests are 789 passing before and after, same set. Reverting just the `i18n.py` line fails exactly the 26 updated expectations and nothing else, so the tests are pinned to the change, not to the diff.\n", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/378/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/378/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/346", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/346/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/346/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/346/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/346", "id": 4821354694, "node_id": "PR_kwDOG9EFvM7udOVy", "number": 346, "title": "Fix intword() rounding carry for very large numbers", "user": {"login": "gaoflow", "id": 3355843, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMzNTU4NDM=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3355843?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow", "html_url": "https://github.com/gaoflow", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gaoflow/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 2, "created_at": "2026-07-06T17:00:50Z", "updated_at": "2026-07-06T17:07:48Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/pulls/346", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/346", "diff_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/346.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/346.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "### Problem\n\n`intword()` decides whether rounding pushed a value up into the next magnitude\nwith:\n\n```python\nif not largest_ordinal and rounded_value * power == powers[ordinal + 1]:\n```\n\nFor values above ~`10**22`, `rounded_value * power` is evaluated in floating\npoint and no longer equals the exact `powers[ordinal + 1]`, so the carry is\nskipped and the number is rendered against the *lower* magnitude:\n\n```python\n>>> import humanize\n>>> humanize.intword(10**24 - 1)\n'1000.0 sextillion'      # expected '1.0 septillion'\n>>> humanize.intword(10**27 - 1)\n'1000.0 septillion'      # expected '1.0 octillion'\n```\n\nThe same happens at `10**30` and `10**33`.\n\n### Fix\n\nCompare `rounded_value` against the exact integer ratio\n`powers[ordinal + 1] // power`, keeping the check in exact integer terms rather\nthan relying on a large float product. This mirrors the recently fixed carry\nhandling in `metric()` (#328) and `naturalsize()` (#329).\n\n### Tests\n\n`test_intword_rounding_rollover` asserts the correct roll-over across every\naffected magnitude (`10**24/27/30/33 - 1`), plus a couple of just-below cases\nthat must *not* roll over, guarding both directions.\n\n`pytest` → 716 passed. `ruff check` / `ruff format --check` clean.\n", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/346/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/346/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/184", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/184/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/184/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/184/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/issues/184", "id": 2260201200, "node_id": "I_kwDOG9EFvM6Gt-7w", "number": 184, "title": "Suggestion: Add an entrypoint and/or scripts for command-line use", "user": {"login": "sakurai-youhei", "id": 721858, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjcyMTg1OA==", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/721858?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei", "html_url": "https://github.com/sakurai-youhei", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sakurai-youhei/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 1, "created_at": "2024-04-24T03:07:13Z", "updated_at": "2024-04-25T19:03:12Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Thank you for your great project!\r\n\r\nGoogle always guides me to https://stackoverflow.com/a/15485265, which suggests `humanize.naturalsize()`. I'm ok to type in `ipython`, and copy & paste `import humanize` and `humanize.naturalsize()`.\r\n\r\nBut it'd be more than great if this small task could be simplified in something like these ways.\r\n\r\n```console\r\n$ naturalsize 8589934592\r\n8.6 GB\r\n$ naturalsize --binary 8589934592\r\n8.0 GiB\r\n$ echo 8589934592 | python -m humanize naturalsize --format \"%.3f\"\r\n8.590 GB\r\n```\r\n\r\nThere are tools such as `numfmt`, but `pip install` is easier for me as a Windows user. :)\r\n\r\nI'd open a PR if I found some time for this. But I can't promise my contribution. So, I'm filing just an idea here.", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/184/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/184/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "pinned_comment": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/357", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/357/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/357/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/357/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/357", "id": 4958548199, "node_id": "PR_kwDOG9EFvM71WZs2", "number": 357, "title": "Fix French decimal separator and apply to `naturalsize`", "user": {"login": "SpiliosDimakopoulos", "id": 150211937, "node_id": "U_kgDOCPQNYQ", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/150211937?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos", "html_url": "https://github.com/SpiliosDimakopoulos", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SpiliosDimakopoulos/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [{"id": 4034495680, "node_id": "LA_kwDOG9EFvM7weYTA", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/labels/changelog:%20Fixed", "name": "changelog: Fixed", "color": "00A800", "default": false, "description": "For any bug fixes"}], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 5, "created_at": "2026-07-23T11:54:55Z", "updated_at": "2026-07-23T13:44:19Z", "closed_at": "2026-07-23T12:38:13Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/pulls/357", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/357", "diff_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/357.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/357.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "Re: #51", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/357/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/357/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/349", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/349/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/349/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/349/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/349", "id": 4847645793, "node_id": "PR_kwDOG9EFvM7vzDso", "number": 349, "title": "filesize: raise ValueError for non-finite bytes in naturalsize", "user": {"login": "HrachShah", "id": 177451801, "node_id": "U_kgDOCpOzGQ", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177451801?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah", "html_url": "https://github.com/HrachShah", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/HrachShah/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 1, "created_at": "2026-07-09T15:33:01Z", "updated_at": "2026-07-09T15:53:31Z", "closed_at": "2026-07-09T15:46:04Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/pulls/349", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/349", "diff_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/349.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/349.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "**Bug**\n\n`naturalsize(float('nan'))` raised `ValueError: cannot convert float NaN to integer` from inside the `int(min(log(...)))` exponent calculation, which is several levels removed from the call site. `naturalsize(float('inf'))` and `naturalsize(float('-inf'))` silently rendered as `'inf QB'` / `'-inf QB'`, which is not a meaningful byte count for any real caller.\n\n**Fix**\n\nReject NaN, +inf, and -inf up front with a single `math.isfinite(bytes_)` check that names the rejected value in the error message. The same check covers string inputs that `float()` accepts but that don't represent a meaningful byte count (`'inf'`, `'INF'`, `'NaN'`, etc.); non-numeric strings still reach the existing `float()` call and raise ValueError as before.\n\n**Tests**\n\nEight new cases in `tests/test_filesize.py`:\n- `test_naturalsize_rejects_non_finite`: parametrized over `float('nan')`, `float('inf')`, `float('-inf')`.\n- `test_naturalsize_rejects_non_finite_strings`: parametrized over `'nan'`, `'inf'`, `'-inf'`, `'NaN'`, `'INF'`.\n\nBoth assert that `pytest.raises(ValueError, match='finite number of bytes')` fires, so the fix is checked end-to-end on every relevant shape of non-finite input.\n\nThree new doctest cases in `naturalsize`: `naturalsize(0)` (the `abs < base` path was previously untested), and explicit `Traceback` / `ValueError` cases for `naturalsize(float('nan'))` and `naturalsize(float('inf'))`.\n\nFull suite: 723 passed, 69 skipped (no regressions).", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/349/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/349/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/329", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/329/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/329/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/329/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/329", "id": 4686243308, "node_id": "PR_kwDOG9EFvM7noLbp", "number": 329, "title": "Fix `naturalsize()` rounding rollover at unit boundaries", "user": {"login": "patchwright", "id": 292882882, "node_id": "U_kgDOEXUJwg", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/292882882?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright", "html_url": "https://github.com/patchwright", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/patchwright/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [{"id": 4034495680, "node_id": "LA_kwDOG9EFvM7weYTA", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/labels/changelog:%20Fixed", "name": "changelog: Fixed", "color": "00A800", "default": false, "description": "For any bug fixes"}], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 3, "created_at": "2026-06-17T19:03:42Z", "updated_at": "2026-06-30T15:36:42Z", "closed_at": "2026-06-30T15:36:42Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/pulls/329", "html_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/329", "diff_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/329.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/python-humanize/humanize/pull/329.patch", "merged_at": "2026-06-30T15:36:42Z"}, "body": "### Problem\n\n`naturalsize()` picks the suffix from the **unrounded** byte count (`exp = int(min(log(abs_bytes, base), ...))`), then rounds the mantissa with the `format` string afterward. When rounding pushes the mantissa up to the base, the already-chosen suffix is left stale:\n\n```pycon\n>>> from humanize import naturalsize\n>>> naturalsize(999999)\n'1000.0 kB'      # expected '1.0 MB'\n>>> naturalsize(999999999)\n'1000.0 MB'      # expected '1.0 GB'\n>>> naturalsize(1024 ** 2 - 1, binary=True)\n'1024.0 KiB'     # expected '1.0 MiB'\n```\n\n`999999` bytes is `999.999 kB`; `\"%.1f\"` rounds that to `1000.0`, but the suffix was already fixed at `kB`, so the output reads `1000.0 kB` instead of `1.0 MB`. This happens at every decimal, binary, and GNU boundary.\n\nThis is **distinct** from the two related changes already in the repo:\n\n- **#206** (closed #205) fixed the `ZB → YB` *top* boundary by adding larger suffixes (`RB`/`QB`); it never touched the rounding logic, so small-unit rollover remained.\n- **#328** fixes the same class in `metric()` — a different function in `number.py`.\n\n### Fix\n\nAfter rounding, if the mantissa has reached the base (`1000` decimal / `1024` binary) **and** a larger suffix is available, step up one suffix. Values already at the largest suffix (`QB`/`QiB`) are unaffected (e.g. the documented `naturalsize(10**34 * 3)` → `'30000.0 QB'` still holds), as are all values that don't round across a boundary.\n\n### Tests\n\nAdded regression assertions to `test_naturalsize` covering decimal, binary, and GNU boundaries. They fail on the current code and pass with this change; every existing assertion and documented example is unchanged (70 → 76 passing).\n", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/329/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/python-humanize/humanize/issues/329/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null, "score": 1.0}], "search_type": "lexical"}